CLASS_ROLES = [('clock', 'Action economy'), ('damage', 'Damage'), ('control', 'Control'), ('shieldmagic', 'Defense'), ('position', 'Mobility'), ('utility', 'Versatility')]
SKILL_ROLES = [('damage', 'Combat'), ('mind', 'Knowledge'), ('talk', 'Social'), ('compass', 'Exploration'), ('position', 'Mobility'), ('shieldmagic', 'Defense')]
DED_ROLES = [('occult', 'Occult casting'), ('damage', 'Combat'), ('utility', 'Utility'), ('team', 'Party role'), ('upgrade', 'Follow-ups'), ('star', 'Flavour')]

# name: (ratings, grade, plan label, evaluation)
F = {}
def f(n, r, g, plan, ev):
    F[n] = (r, g, plan, ev)

# ── Class feats ──
f("Magus's Analysis", '400003', 'S', 'Taken at 1 (Natural Ambition)', "Magus's Analysis combines a Recall Knowledge check with a recharge for a single action, so the action Cyrus would spend recharging also tells him and his allies something useful. It is strongest when it follows a Spellstrike on the same target, because the earlier hit gives a +1 bonus to the check, he learns which save or weakness to aim at next, and he ends the turn with Spellstrike recharged. Each creature can be analysed only once a day, so against a single powerful enemy he can use it once in the fight, while against a group he can use it on a different enemy each turn.")
f('Force Fang', '420002', 'A', 'Taken at 2', "Force Fang adds a second conflux spell and therefore a second Focus Point, which is its most important benefit. The spell recharges Spellstrike for one action while dealing force damage that cannot miss, so it is a better way to recharge than the ordinary action whenever the target is in reach. It has the manipulate trait, so casting it inside an enemy's reach can provoke Reactive Strike. When movement matters more than damage, the Focus Point is better spent on Dimensional Assault.")
f('Expansive Spellstrike', '043003', 'S', 'Planned at 4', "Expansive Spellstrike restores the area of burst, cone and line spells delivered through Spellstrike, so a Spellstrike can hit a group as well as its target. With a reach weapon, cones and lines start from any square adjacent to the target rather than from Cyrus, which makes it much easier to aim them away from himself and his allies. It is also the feat that makes Sprinting Spellstrike's line follow his movement at level 12, so in practice he needs it for the combination his later turns depend on.")
f('Running Recharge', '500040', 'A', 'Alternative at 16, or at 8 without the stave', "Running Recharge recharges Spellstrike and lets Cyrus Stride half his Speed or Step for one action, which fixes the magus problem of choosing between moving and recharging on the third action. It is the right pick at 8 if Aspera's stave isn't ready for Fused Staff. At 16 it competes with Arcane Shroud; once Cyrus is regularly quickened, the extra movement matters less, and Arcane Shroud's defensive buff becomes the better use of the slot.")
f("Striker's Scroll", '210002', 'C', 'Not planned', "Striker's Scroll lets Cyrus attach a scroll to Aspera and cast it through Spellstrike, including occult scrolls after his dedication. In principle that gives him more spells to put into a Spellstrike without spending slots. In practice it occupies the place on Aspera where a talisman or spellheart goes, which is better used for the Clay Sphere, and each use consumes a scroll, so it is expensive for what it adds.")
f('Burning Cascade', '020000', 'C', 'Not planned', "Burning Cascade deals Arcane Cascade's extra damage to every enemy within 5 feet when Cyrus enters the stance. Because he fights from 10-foot reach, most enemies are outside the emanation when he enters stance, and each enemy can only be affected once a minute. It therefore offers him little.")
f('Distracting Spellstrike', '220000', 'F', 'Unavailable with Aspera', "Distracting Spellstrike requires a free hand and adds a Feint, which uses Deception. Cyrus fights with both hands on Aspera and has a low Charisma, so he cannot meet the requirement and would gain little if he could.")
f('Reactive Strike', '034200', 'S', 'Planned at 6', "Reactive Strike is the feat that makes a reach weapon work for Cyrus. With 10-foot reach he threatens a large area, and any enemy that moves through it, uses a manipulate action or makes a ranged attack inside it can be struck at full accuracy without affecting his multiple attack penalty. It also combines well with tripping, because a prone enemy that stands up provokes the reaction. A critical hit disrupts a triggering manipulate action, which can stop an enemy spell.")
f('Spell Crash', '330002', 'B', 'Alternative at 6', "Spell Crash spends a prepared spell slot to create a force blast in a 20-foot emanation, 30-foot cone or 60-foot line, dealing damage based on the slot's rank. Because Aspera has the trip trait, every creature that fails its save also falls prone. With one or two fights in a day Cyrus often has slots to spare, which makes this more appealing than it would be on a day of many fights. Its damage still depends on saves against his spell DC, and Reactive Strike is of use in every round.")
f("Conjurer's Countermeasure", '200300', 'B', 'Alternative at 6', "Conjurer's Countermeasure is a conflux spell that grants resistance 5 to spell damage, stacking with Arcane Cascade's resistance. As a conflux spell it also recharges Spellstrike when cast and adds a Focus Point. It is a strong choice when enemy spellcasters are common, but Reactive Strike is the better feat for general use at this level.")
f('Knowledge is Power', '000101', 'C', 'Not planned', "Knowledge is Power grants small bonuses after a critical success on Recall Knowledge. Critical successes are too uncertain to rely on and the bonuses are minor, so it is a poor use of a class feat.")
f('Spell Retaliation', '300000', 'C', 'Not planned', "Spell Retaliation recharges Spellstrike as a free action when Cyrus succeeds at a save against an enemy spell or an enemy spell attack misses him. It only helps in fights against spellcasters and depends on the enemy acting first, so it applies too rarely to be worth a class feat.")
f('Fused Staff', '200005', 'A', 'Planned at 8 if the stave is ready', "Fused Staff merges a magical staff into Aspera, so Cyrus can cast the staff's spells while holding his weapon in both hands, and the fused item uses the higher of the two items' fundamental runes. Its value lies entirely in the staff's spell list, which is why he takes it at the level at which Aspera's own stave becomes available. With one or two fights in a day, the staff's daily charges are divided among very few encounters, so more of them can be spent in each.")
f('Standby Spell', '000004', 'B', 'Alternative at 8', "Standby Spell lets Cyrus cast one chosen Spellstrike spell from any slot of high enough rank without preparing it. It helps if he often finds the right spell unprepared, but with careful preparation each morning and few fights in a day, that happens less often.")
f('Runic Impression', '330003', 'B', 'Alternative at 8', "Runic Impression is a conflux spell that gives Aspera a chosen property rune, such as flaming, frost or ghost touch, for a short time. It also recharges Spellstrike and adds a Focus Point. It is a flexible answer to resistances and incorporeal enemies, but taking it at this level would mean giving up Fused Staff.")
f('Spell Swipe', '320000', 'C', 'Not planned', "Spell Swipe makes a Spellstrike against two adjacent creatures within reach for three actions. It leaves no action for moving or recharging, and the targets must be adjacent to each other, so it rarely fits Cyrus's turn.")
f('Capture Magic', '100200', 'C', 'Not planned', "Capture Magic lets Cyrus enter or boost Arcane Cascade as a reaction after resisting an enemy spell. It uses the reaction he keeps for Reactive Strike and applies only against spellcasters.")
f('Dimensional Disappearance', '320450', 'S', 'Planned at 10', "Dimensional Disappearance makes Cyrus invisible after every Dimensional Assault. He can skip the Strike to stay hidden and reposition safely, or make the Strike against an enemy that can't see him, which leaves it off-guard and brings Laughing Shadow's increased damage. That makes it both his best means of escape and his best opening attack, and it reduces his need to prepare Invisibility. The elusive, teleporting way in which Cyrus fights depends on it.")
f('Cascading Ray', '300001', 'B', 'Alternative at 10 or 16', "Cascading Ray lets Cyrus follow a successful Spellstrike that dealt energy damage with a one-action ray against a second enemy within 120 feet. It uses his spell attack at the same multiple attack penalty as the Strike, so it misses more often than Aspera would, but it is a reasonable use of a spare third action.")
f('Rapid Recharge', '300000', 'B', 'Alternative', "Rapid Recharge recharges Spellstrike as a free action once per day. With one or two fights in a day that comes close to once in each fight, which makes it better for Cyrus than it usually is. It still offers less than Dimensional Disappearance at level 10.")
f('Sprinting Spellstrike', '440060', 'S', 'Planned at 12', "Sprinting Spellstrike is central to the way Cyrus fights from level 12, because it adds to his mobility and his damage at once. He moves in a straight line up to the length of a line spell, passing through enemies without triggering reactions, and then makes his Spellstrike. With Expansive Spellstrike, the spell's line follows his movement, so every enemy along the path is hit by the spell. It combines well with Lightning Bolt and Blazing Fissure, and also with Living Thunderbolt, whose fly Speed the movement can use and which damages every creature he passes through.")
f('Conflux Focus', '300002', 'C', 'Not planned', "Conflux Focus refills Cyrus's whole focus pool whenever he Refocuses. With one or two fights in a day and time to rest between them, an ordinary Refocus already restores most or all of the pool before the next fight. The feat would matter only on long days with several fights in succession.")
f('Overwhelming Spellstrike', '300000', 'C', 'Not planned', "Overwhelming Spellstrike ignores energy resistance equal to Cyrus's level for one Spellstrike. Arcane Cascade's choice of damage type and a varied set of prepared spells usually solve the same problem.")
f('Magic Sense (Magus)', '000003', 'C', 'Not planned', "Magic Sense gives Cyrus a permanent 1st-rank Detect Magic in his field of vision. Detect Magic is already a cantrip, and one that other casters among his allies have, so a class feat is too high a price.")
f('Hasted Assault', '500030', 'A', 'Planned at 14', "Hasted Assault is a conflux spell that makes Cyrus quickened for a minute, with the extra action usable for Stride or Strike, and it recharges Spellstrike when cast. Cast in the first round, it gives him an extra action every turn of the fight, close to a permanent Haste on himself. It doesn't stack with Haste, which frees the party's Haste for Mira or Cassius. It also adds a third Focus Point.")
f('Arcane Shroud', '303433', 'A', 'Planned at 16', "Arcane Shroud turns every entry into Arcane Cascade into a short buff: Cyrus picks one of his three chosen spells each time and keeps it until the end of his next turn. By 16 he is often quickened from Haste, Hasted Assault or an ally, which covers the movement that Running Recharge was meant to provide and leaves a normal action free to re-enter the stance. Invisibility is the strongest pick: re-entered as the last action of a turn, it forces a DC 11 flat check on every attack against him until his next hostile action, and the Strike that ends it is made while he is hidden, so the target is off-guard and Laughing Shadow applies. Fleet Step and See the Unseen are the other useful choices, and False Vitality gives temporary Hit Points that can be refreshed for one action. It has two limits that matter. He gets one of the three spells each time, not all three, and a stance can be entered only during an encounter, so the feat gives no invisibility for scouting outside combat. The stance trait also limits him to entering it once a round.")
f('Dispelling Spellstrike', '020003', 'C', 'Not planned', "Dispelling Spellstrike adds a counteract attempt to a three-action Spellstrike. A scroll of Dispel Magic, or another caster among his allies, deals with enemy spells and wards at less cost.")
f('Resounding Cascade', '210200', 'B', 'Alternative at 16', "Resounding Cascade extends Arcane Cascade's base extra damage and resistance to allies within 5 feet of Cyrus. Because he fights from 10-foot reach, his allies are often not within 5 feet, which limits its value for him.")

# ── Skill and general feats ──
f('Fleet', '300050', 'S', 'Taken at 1 (Versatile Human)', "Fleet adds 5 feet to Cyrus's Speed, and almost everything he does depends on Speed. Dimensional Assault teleports him up to half his Speed before level 9 and his full Speed afterwards, so Fleet lengthens every teleport, as well as every Stride to a flanking square and every approach before a Sprinting Spellstrike. It adds to Laughing Shadow's bonus and to the bonus from boots, and it costs nothing to use. His turns depend on reaching the right square, so no other general feat adds as much to every fight.")
f('Canny Acumen', '302302', 'A', 'Taken at 1 (background)', "Canny Acumen makes Cyrus an expert in Perception from level 1, eight levels before his class would. He rolls Perception for initiative, so in a hard fight it helps to decide whether he trips or weakens the most dangerous enemy before it acts. It is also the roll for noticing ambushes and hidden creatures during exploration, and for Sense Motive in conversation. His class reaches expert at 9, but the feat then takes him to master at 17, so it remains useful at both low and high levels.")
f('Additional Lore', '350000', 'S', 'Taken (Academia from the campaign, Warfare at 2)', "Additional Lore raises its chosen Lore to expert at 3, master at 7 and legendary at 15 without spending skill increases. That is how Cyrus keeps two strong Lores while still raising Athletics and Arcana. Improvise Strategy requires Warfare Lore at master, which he reaches at 7, so this feat supports the way he fights as well as his learning.")
f('Toughness', '100004', 'A', 'Taken at 3', "Toughness adds Hit Points equal to Cyrus's level and lowers the DC of recovery checks. He fights among the enemy, ends his turns close to his target and spends his actions on Spellstrike instead of defence, so it is in hard fights that he is most likely to fall. More Hit Points in every fight, and a better chance of stabilising when he does fall, make it one of the most dependable general feats for him. It does nothing else, which is the only reason it is not graded higher.")
f('Incredible Initiative', '400000', 'A', 'Planned at 5 (General Training)', "Incredible Initiative gives +2 to initiative rolls. Acting before the enemy lets Cyrus trip or weaken its most dangerous member before his allies act, and take up a good position before his side can be surrounded.")
f("Kreighton's Cognitive Crossover", '150100', 'A', 'Planned at 4', "Kreighton's Cognitive Crossover lets Cyrus retry a failed Recall Knowledge check with a second chosen skill as a reaction. With Arcana paired with Academia Lore or Society, he learns nothing far less often when he tries to identify an enemy, an artefact or a historical clue. It also gives Magus's Analysis a second chance in combat, although there it uses the reaction he keeps for Reactive Strike. It is a legacy feat that was not reprinted, so it remains available.")
f('Magical Shorthand', '030200', 'A', 'Planned at 6', "Magical Shorthand turns every successful Learn a Spell check into a critical success, which halves the cost, and makes learning any spell take 10 minutes regardless of rank. Gold is what Cyrus is shortest of, because runes, Aspera's stave and his invested items all have to be paid for, so halving the cost of every spell he adds to his spellbook saves a great deal over time. The 10-minute learning time matters as much, because it lets him copy a scroll or a captured spellbook during a short rest instead of waiting for free days. When he does have free days, the option to learn spells in place of earning income is a further benefit.")
f('Improvise Strategy', '500000', 'S', 'Planned at 7', "Improvise Strategy costs one action and uses Warfare Lore against a creature's Perception DC, so it leaves Cyrus's first attack free for the Strike or Trip that follows. On a success the target is clumsy, dazzled, off-guard or stupefied until the end of his next turn. The off-guard condition brings Laughing Shadow's increased damage, and the clumsy condition makes the Trip that follows easier. It begins the turn he most often wants to take, which is Improvise Strategy, then a Trip, then Dimensional Assault.")
f('Battle Planner', '200000', 'C', 'Not planned', "Battle Planner lets Cyrus spend a minute planning and use a Warfare Lore roll as his initiative if the plan still holds. It works only when there is time to scout beforehand, and Incredible Initiative improves his initiative more reliably.")
f('Unmistakable Lore', '050200', 'A', 'Planned at 8', "Unmistakable Lore removes critical failures on Recall Knowledge with any Lore Cyrus is trained in, and gives extra information on critical successes once he is a master. A critical failure on Recall Knowledge gives false information, which is worse than none when others act on it. As the scholar among his allies, with several Lores from Additional Lore and Aspera's gifts, he makes these checks often in both investigation and combat, so the protection is in regular use.")
f('Courtly Graces', '005200', 'A', 'Planned at 10', "Courtly Graces lets Cyrus use Society to make an impression on nobles and to impersonate them. In a campaign driven by roleplay, with the party tied into Cormyrean noble houses through Cassius, it gives him a dependable social tool built on his strongest Intelligence skill rather than Charisma. It also matches his background as a scholar who understands courtly etiquette. It has no use in combat, which matters little for a skill feat.")
f('Leverage Connections', '004200', 'B', 'Alternative at 12', "Leverage Connections lets Cyrus call in favours from contacts once a week. Where he has noble and academic acquaintances whom he meets repeatedly, it is a real source of information, access and introductions. Its value depends on how often he returns to places where he knows people.")
f('Titan Wrestler', '400000', 'A', 'Planned at 12', "Titan Wrestler lets Cyrus Trip, Grapple, Shove, Reposition and Disarm creatures two sizes larger than him, or three at legendary Athletics. From level 12 many of the most dangerous enemies are Huge or larger, and without this feat he could not Trip them at all, so it keeps his tripping effective at high level.")
f('Quick Jump', '000020', 'C', 'Alternative', "Quick Jump turns High Jump and Long Jump into single actions without a run-up. It helps on vertical maps, but Dimensional Assault and Time Jump cover most of the same movement.")
f('Bon Mot', '310000', 'C', 'Alternative', "Bon Mot imposes a penalty to Will saves and Perception for one action, which helps allies whose spells target Will. It uses Diplomacy, and Cyrus's Charisma is low, so it is less reliable for him than Improvise Strategy.")
f('Unified Theory', '050300', 'A', 'Planned at 15', "Unified Theory lets legendary Arcana stand in for Nature, Occultism and Religion on checks about magic. That lets Cyrus answer questions about every magical item, effect, ward or creature with his best skill. Where there is a great deal to investigate, it means the answer no longer depends on whoever happens to have the matching skill.")
f('Trick Magic Item', '000300', 'C', 'Not planned', "Trick Magic Item lets Cyrus try to activate items from traditions he can't cast. The Witch or Psychic dedication gives him occult casting directly, which covers most items he would want.")
f('Prescient Planner', '000300', 'C', 'Not planned', "Prescient Planner lets Cyrus retrieve a common item he didn't pack, for its price. It needs a second feat to cover consumables, and a well-chosen kit covers most of the same needs.")
f('Prescient Consumable', '000300', 'C', 'Not planned', "Prescient Consumable extends Prescient Planner to consumables. Two feats for flexible shopping is a poor trade compared with planning the kit.")
f('Biographical Eye', '003100', 'B', 'Not planned', "Biographical Eye lets Cyrus infer a stranger's background after a minute of observation. In a campaign with a lot of intrigue it gives useful leverage before a conversation starts, but it needs a minute and a willing GM to pay off, so it is a good free pick rather than a priority.")
f("Axuma's Awakening", '200300', 'B', 'Planned at 11 (reflavoured)', "Axuma's Awakening gives two arcane cantrips at will and one rank 1 and one rank 2 spell once a day, all as innate spells keyed to Charisma. Cyrus's Charisma is low, so the right picks are spells that need no attack roll or save. Sure Strike at rank 1 makes one Spellstrike a fortune roll; Hidebound or Warping Pull at rank 2 are reactions that protect an ally from a hit; Lucky Number is the alternative if he would rather keep a once-a-day reroll for himself. For the cantrips, Shield, Message and Telekinetic Hand free his prepared cantrips for damage. It is a good general feat at 11 because it adds a fortune effect and a reaction without costing slots, but none of it changes his turn the way a class feat does.")
f('Assurance', '200000', 'C', 'Not planned', "Assurance gives a fixed result on Athletics checks. Cyrus's Athletics bonus is high, so rolling usually gives a better result.")
f('Kip Up', '000030', 'C', 'Not planned', "Kip Up lets Cyrus stand without provoking reactions. It helps against enemies that trip, but it is a narrow defensive feat.")
f('Combat Climber', '000020', 'C', 'Not planned', "Combat Climber removes the off-guard condition while climbing. Gecko Grip becomes a studious spell at 7 and covers most climbing needs.")
f('Powerful Leap', '000020', 'C', 'Not planned', "Powerful Leap increases jump distance. Time Jump and Fly provide much more movement.")

# ── Ancestry ──
f('Natural Ambition', '400000', 'S', 'Taken at 1', "Natural Ambition gave Cyrus Magus's Analysis at level 1, a feat he uses in every fight.")
f('General Training', '300000', 'A', 'Planned at 5', "General Training grants a level-1 general feat. Incredible Initiative is the planned choice, improving Cyrus's chance of acting before the enemy.")
f('Clever Improviser', '002200', 'B', 'Alternative at 13', "Clever Improviser lets Cyrus attempt actions that normally need training and improves his untrained checks. It suits a generalist scholar who is often asked to try unfamiliar tasks.")
f('Multitalented', '300003', 'A', 'Planned at 9', "Multitalented grants a multiclass dedication feat without its usual requirements. It is how Cyrus gains occult casting, which fills the party's missing tradition.")
f('Advanced General Training', '300000', 'B', 'Alternative at 13', "Advanced General Training grants a general feat of level 7 or lower, such as a second skill feat or Prescient Consumable.")

# ── Dedications at 9 ──
f('Witch Dedication', '514534', 'S', 'Recommended at 9', "Witch Dedication gives Cyrus the occult Cast a Spell activity, which lets him use occult scrolls, wands and Aspera's stave, including Synesthesia. Under the remastered rules he uses his existing spell attack and spell DC rather than a weaker trained value, so his occult items are as effective as his arcane spells. It also gives him a familiar with two occult cantrips, such as Guidance and Read the Air, and the familiar's own abilities. That makes him the party's occult caster without spending any further feats.")
f('Psychic Dedication', '533523', 'A', 'Alternative at 9', "Psychic Dedication grants the same occult casting access as the Witch dedication, plus one psi cantrip from a chosen conscious mind. Some psi cantrips are attack spells that work through Spellstrike. It has no familiar, so it trades utility for combat value. Choose it if the extra combat cantrip matters more than a familiar.")
f('Rogue Dedication', '030202', 'C', 'Not recommended', "Rogue Dedication requires Dexterity +2, which Cyrus doesn't plan to have. Its Surprise Attack and extra skill feat don't address the party's needs.")
f('Exemplar Dedication', '040113', 'B', 'Flavour option', "Exemplar Dedication grants an ikon with its own empowered effects, which suits a character whose weapon is a growing relic. It adds no occult casting, so the party would still lack an occult caster.")
f('Commander Dedication', '030445', 'A', 'Flavour option', "Commander Dedication grants Intelligence-based tactics that move or empower allies, and its Warfare Lore theme fits Cyrus closely. It is a strong team option, but it doesn't give occult casting, so the party would still lack an occult caster.")


# ── plan as of level 4: campaign bonus feats, the level-20 build, and evaluations that name no party member ──
def _relabel(n, plan, old=None, new=None, grade=None):
    r, g, _p, ev = F[n]
    if old is not None:
        assert old in ev, n
        ev = ev.replace(old, new)
    F[n] = (r, grade or g, plan, ev)

_relabel('Expansive Spellstrike', 'Taken at 4')
_relabel('Fused Staff', 'Planned at 8')
_relabel('Witch Dedication', 'Planned at 9')
_relabel('Unified Theory', 'Planned at 16')
_relabel('Leverage Connections', 'Alternative at 14')
_relabel('Clever Improviser', 'Alternative at 13')
_relabel('Quick Jump', 'Planned at 14', "but Dimensional Assault and Time Jump cover most of the same movement.",
         "but Dimensional Assault and Time Jump cover most of the same movement. It is the base for Cloud Jump at 18, which is where the pair becomes worth using.")
_relabel('Arcane Shroud', 'Planned at 16', "which covers the movement that Running Recharge was meant to provide and leaves a normal action free to re-enter the stance.",
         "which covers his movement and leaves a normal action free to re-enter the stance.")
_relabel('Hasted Assault', 'Planned at 14', "which frees the party's Haste for Mira or Cassius. It also adds a third Focus Point.",
         "which frees the party's Haste for another melee ally. It also adds a third Focus Point. From level 20 Supreme Spellstrike makes him permanently quickened, so Hasted Assault then adds only Stride as a use for the extra action, alongside its Focus Point and its recharge.")
f('Running Recharge', '500040', 'A', 'Taken at 4 (campaign bonus class feat)', "Running Recharge recharges Spellstrike and lets Cyrus Stride half his Speed or Step for one action, which spares him the choice every magus faces between moving and recharging with the third action. He can use Running Recharge to reach a flanking square and then Spellstrike, without spending a Focus Point. It is the way to recharge when Magus's Analysis has already been used on the target and he needs to move. When the target is already in reach and flanked, Force Fang adds damage for the same action.")
f('Courtly Graces', '005200', 'A', 'Planned at 10', "Courtly Graces lets Cyrus use Society to make an impression on nobles and to impersonate them. It gives him a dependable social tool in any scene set among nobility, based on an Intelligence skill instead of on Charisma. It also matches his background as a scholar who understands courtly etiquette. It has no use in combat, which matters little for a skill feat.")
f('Prescient Planner', '000300', 'C', 'Taken at 3 (campaign bonus general feat)', "Prescient Planner lets Cyrus spend a minute to produce a common piece of adventuring gear he had not declared buying, for its price, once between each chance to shop. The item's level can be no higher than half his own, and it cannot be a weapon, armour, an alchemical item or a magic item. On its own it only covers mundane gear, such as rope, tools or a ladder. Cyrus takes it with the campaign's bonus general feat because it is the prerequisite for Prescient Consumable at 13.")
f('Prescient Consumable', '000400', 'B', 'Planned at 13 (Advanced General Training)', "Prescient Consumable lets Prescient Planner produce a common consumable in place of adventuring gear: a scroll, potion, talisman or similar item of a level no higher than half his own, for its price. At 13 that reaches level-6 items, such as a rank-3 scroll, and at 20 level-10 items, such as a rank-5 scroll. For a prepared caster with two slots of each rank, one unplanned scroll is a way to have a spell he did not prepare, including occult scrolls after the dedication. It takes a minute, so it is used before a fight or during exploration, and it works once between each chance to shop. It costs two feats in total, which is why it is graded below the feats that work in every fight.")
f('Advanced General Training', '300000', 'B', 'Planned at 13', "Advanced General Training grants a general feat of level 7 or lower. Cyrus uses it for Prescient Consumable, which needs Prescient Planner from level 3.")
f('Stolen Spell', '240003', 'A', 'Planned at 18', "Stolen Spell triggers as a free action when Cyrus critically succeeds at a save against an enemy's spell, or an enemy critically fails a spell attack roll against him. Twofold Will from level 9 and Spell-Tempered Body from 15 turn every success on a Will or Fortitude save into a critical success, so any Will or Fortitude spell he saves against triggers it. He can then cast that spell once before the end of his next turn at no cost, even if it is not an arcane spell or is of a higher rank than he can cast. If he delivers it through Spellstrike to the creature that cast it, that creature is off-guard against the Strike.")
f('Supreme Spellstrike', '640000', 'S', 'Planned at 20', "Supreme Spellstrike makes Cyrus permanently quickened, with the extra action limited to a Strike or to recharging Spellstrike. A free recharge every turn means a Spellstrike every round, with the third action left for moving, Magus's Analysis, a conflux spell or Arcane Cascade. Aspera's planned grand gift at 17 removes the limit on what the extra action can be used for. Quickened from several sources still gives one extra action, so from this level Haste and Hasted Assault only add more ways to use it.")
f('Cloud Jump', '100240', 'B', 'Planned at 18', "Cloud Jump triples the distance of a Long Jump and lets a High Jump use Long Jump distances, and extra actions extend a jump beyond his Speed. With Quick Jump, one action carries Cyrus up to his full Speed across a gap, a hazard or difficult terrain on a check he passes easily at legendary Athletics, or straight up to a ledge. It costs no spell slot or Focus Point. Fly and Dimensional Assault cover much of the same ground, so its value is on maps with height and broken terrain, and it needs Quick Jump to be worth an action in a fight.")
f('Legendary Professional', '003100', 'C', 'Planned at 20', "Legendary Professional makes Cyrus famous for one of his Lores. People with any knowledge of Society have heard of him and usually start one step friendlier, and he finds higher-level work when he Earns Income with that Lore. It has no effect in a fight. It fits a level-20 scholar and tactician, and by 20 the skill feats that matter in combat are already taken.")
f('Heroic Presence', '300003', 'B', 'Planned at 17', "Once a day, for one action, Heroic Presence gives up to 10 willing creatures within 30 feet the effects of a 6th-rank Zealous Conviction: 12 temporary Hit Points and a +2 status bonus to Will saves against mental effects for 10 minutes. It is a party-wide effect for a single action, from a spell that is not on the arcane list. The temporary Hit Points are small at level 17, so most of its value is the Will bonus in fights with fear, control or other mental effects.")
f('Sanguine Tenacity', '000003', 'B', 'Planned at 19', "Sanguine Tenacity treats enfeebled and drained as 1 lower when working out their penalties and the Hit Points that drained removes. It also gives resistance 5 to persistent bleed damage and makes that damage easier to end. Enfeebled lowers attack rolls, damage and Athletics checks, so ignoring enfeebled 1 protects both Spellstrike and Trip. It needs Constitution +4, which the plan reaches at 15. It only matters against enemies that inflict those conditions.")
_relabel("Kreighton's Cognitive Crossover", 'Taken at 4', " It is a legacy feat that was not reprinted, so it remains available.", "")
_relabel('Witch Dedication', 'Planned at 9', "Under the remastered rules he uses his existing spell attack and spell DC rather than a weaker trained value, so his occult items are as effective as his arcane spells.",
         "He uses his existing spell attack and spell DC for them, so his occult items are as effective as his arcane spells.")
_relabel('Toughness', 'Taken at 3')
_relabel('Canny Acumen', 'Taken at 1 (background) and at 15 for Reflex')


# ── Evaluations in their current wording (applied last) ──
def _ev(n, ev):
    r, g, plan, _ = F[n]
    F[n] = (r, g, plan, ev)


_ev('Hasted Assault', "Hasted Assault is a conflux spell that makes Cyrus quickened for a minute, with the extra action usable for a Stride or a Strike, and it recharges Spellstrike when cast. Cast in the first round, it gives him an extra action in every turn of the fight, which is close to having Haste on himself whenever he wants it. The two do not combine, so an ally's Haste can go to someone else who fights in melee. It also adds a third Focus Point. From level 20 Supreme Spellstrike makes him permanently quickened, so Hasted Assault then adds only the Stride as a use for the extra action, along with its Focus Point and its recharge.")
_ev('Arcane Shroud', "Arcane Shroud gives Cyrus a brief spell effect each time he enters Arcane Cascade. He selects one of his three chosen spells each time and keeps it until the end of his next turn. By 16 he is often quickened by Haste, Hasted Assault or an ally, which provides his movement and leaves an ordinary action free for entering the stance again. Invisibility is the strongest of the choices. When he enters the stance with the last action of a turn, every attack against him needs a DC 11 flat check until his next hostile action, and the Strike that ends the invisibility is made while he is hidden, so the target is off-guard and Laughing Shadow's extra damage applies. Fleet Step and See the Unseen are the other useful choices, and False Vitality gives temporary Hit Points that can be renewed for one action. It has two limits that matter. He gets one of the three spells each time, not all three, and a stance can be entered only during an encounter, so the feat gives no invisibility for scouting outside combat. The stance trait also limits him to entering it once a round.")
_ev('Quick Jump', "Quick Jump turns High Jump and Long Jump into single actions without a run-up. It helps where a fight involves height, but Dimensional Assault and Time Jump provide most of the same movement. It is the prerequisite for Cloud Jump at 18, and it is with that feat that the two become worth using.")
_ev('Prescient Planner', "Prescient Planner lets Cyrus spend a minute to produce a common piece of adventuring gear he had not declared buying, for its price, once between each chance to shop. The item's level can be no higher than half his own, and it cannot be a weapon, armour, an alchemical item or a magic item. By itself it covers only mundane gear, such as rope, tools or a ladder. He takes it because it is the prerequisite for Prescient Consumable at 13.")
_ev('Biographical Eye', "Biographical Eye lets Cyrus infer a stranger's background after a minute of observation. Where intrigue is common, that gives him something to work with before a conversation begins, but it needs the minute, and how much he learns varies a good deal, so it is worth taking only when nothing more pressing is available.")
_ev("Axuma's Awakening", "Axuma's Awakening gives two arcane cantrips at will and one rank-1 and one rank-2 spell once a day, all as innate spells that use Charisma. Cyrus's Charisma is low, so the right choices are spells that need no attack roll or save. Sure Strike at rank 1 lets him roll one Spellstrike twice. Hidebound or Warping Pull at rank 2 is a reaction that protects an ally from a hit, and Lucky Number is the alternative if he would sooner keep a daily reroll for himself. Taking Shield, Message or Telekinetic Hand as the cantrips leaves his prepared cantrips free for damage. It is a good general feat at 11 because it adds a second roll and a reaction without using slots, although none of it changes his turn as a class feat does.")
_ev('Kip Up', "Kip Up lets Cyrus stand without provoking reactions. It helps against enemies that trip, but that is a narrow kind of protection for a skill feat.")
_ev('Multitalented', "Multitalented grants a multiclass dedication feat without its usual requirements. It is how Cyrus gains occult spellcasting, the one tradition his allies do not have.")
_ev('Witch Dedication', "Witch Dedication gives Cyrus the ability to cast occult spells, which lets him use occult scrolls, wands and Aspera's stave, including Synesthesia. He uses his existing spell attack and spell DC for them, so his occult items are as effective as his arcane spells. It also gives him a familiar with two occult cantrips, such as Guidance and Read the Air, and the familiar's own abilities. With that one feat he supplies the occult tradition that his allies otherwise lack.")
_ev('Psychic Dedication', "Psychic Dedication grants the same access to occult spellcasting as Witch Dedication, with one psi cantrip from a chosen conscious mind. Some psi cantrips are attack spells that work in a Spellstrike. It gives no familiar, so it offers more in combat and less outside it, and it is the better choice only if the extra cantrip matters more to him than a familiar.")
_ev('Rogue Dedication', "Rogue Dedication requires Dexterity +2, which Cyrus does not intend to have. Its Surprise Attack and extra skill feat add nothing that he or his allies need.")
_ev('Exemplar Dedication', "Exemplar Dedication grants an ikon with empowered effects of its own, which suits a character whose weapon is a growing relic. It adds no occult spellcasting, so his allies would still be without that tradition.")
_ev('Commander Dedication', "Commander Dedication grants tactics based on Intelligence that move or strengthen allies, and its association with Warfare Lore fits Cyrus closely. It would do a great deal for his allies, but it gives no occult spellcasting, so they would still be without that tradition.")
_ev('Heroic Presence', "Once a day, for one action, Heroic Presence gives up to 10 willing creatures within 30 feet the effects of a 6th-rank Zealous Conviction: 12 temporary Hit Points and a +2 status bonus to Will saves against mental effects for 10 minutes. That is a benefit for everyone on his side from a single action, from a spell that is not on the arcane list. The temporary Hit Points are few at level 17, so most of its value lies in the Will bonus in fights that involve fear, control or other mental effects.")
_ev('Sanguine Tenacity', "Sanguine Tenacity treats the enfeebled and drained conditions as 1 lower when their penalties, and the Hit Points that drained removes, are worked out. It also gives resistance 5 to persistent bleed damage and makes that damage easier to end. Enfeebled lowers attack rolls, damage and Athletics checks, so ignoring enfeebled 1 protects both his Spellstrike and his Trip. It needs Constitution +4, which he reaches at 15. It matters only against enemies that inflict those conditions.")
